<title>MEXICO: FORECAST - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 28.23 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 28.23 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 94 basis points to 28.23 percent, and rates are seen mixed at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of 11 Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates with expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     27.29	    28.23		   + 94 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     26.57	    27.11		   + 54 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    25.76	    25.72		   -  4 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     25.59	    25.55		   -  4 bps</p>
<p>The results of this week's auction will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EST.</p>
<p>--Mexico City newsroom, (525) 728-9559</p>
</text>
